url: "https://sparkainlpx.xyz"
abstract: >-
  Max Slate Einstein is an offline-first Python prototype of a bounded
  character engine for an Einstein-inspired educational avatar. It prefers a
  small, deterministic, policy-bounded response over unsupported elaboration.
  It separates persona policy, local source-linked knowledge records, session
  memory policy, routing and safety, and the response pipeline. Historical
  questions go to an evidence-conscious fallback, quote-attribution questions
  to a quote check (VERIFIED, DISPUTED or UNSOURCED), unsafe and professional-
  advice requests to refusal, and topics after 1955 or modern technology to an
  educator mode. Scope: an educational simulation. It does not claim that
  Albert Einstein speaks through it, nor sentience, autonomy or historical
  authenticity. It is not medical, legal, financial or safety-critical
  software, it uses no remote model, and long-term memory is disabled by
  default. Synthetic tests establish deterministic software behaviour only; no
  independent human, historical or security evaluation has been performed.
